  "plain": "Bryce Zabel, a guest on Jesse Michels' podcast, says that after the writer Whitley Strieber published his 1987 book Communion, nearly half a million people wrote letters to Strieber and his wife. Zabel tells it to show how many people the book seemed to reach, and how many may have felt it described something they knew."
